From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thibaut Lapierre <root@epheo.eu>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] healthcheck: no lvms on community

Community builds never deploy LVMS (startCSIPlugin returns early for
them), but the healthcheck still expected openshift-storage whenever the
host had a volume group or /etc/microshift/lvmd.yaml, so greenboot failed
healthy boots. lvmsIsExpected now returns false for the community
variant, and storage config validation keeps running.

Upstream: the deploy is gated on the variant, the healthcheck is not, as
of 5.0.
Covered by: vm-test (a VG exists on every test VM).
---
 pkg/healthcheck/microshift_core_workloads.go | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pkg/healthcheck/microshift_core_workloads.go b/pkg/healthcheck/microshift_core_workloads.go
index 164ddcb3ac8245df71c0e8ed6fa6d6545ad52680..c84d5c4974b5cb82d3e61e3bc46f6c3a34ddd73c 100644
--- a/pkg/healthcheck/microshift_core_workloads.go
+++ b/pkg/healthcheck/microshift_core_workloads.go
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@ import (
 
 	"github.com/openshift/microshift/pkg/config"
 	"github.com/openshift/microshift/pkg/util"
+	"github.com/openshift/microshift/pkg/version"
 	"k8s.io/klog/v2"
 )
 
@@ -45,6 +46,14 @@ func getCoreMicroShiftWorkloads() (map[string]NamespaceWorkloads, error) {
 }
 
 func lvmsIsExpected(cfg *config.Config) (bool, error) {
+	// Community builds never deploy LVMS (startCSIPlugin returns early), so a
+	// volume group or an lvmd.yaml on the host must not arm the expectation:
+	// greenboot would fail a healthy boot waiting for openshift-storage.
+	if version.Get().BuildVariant == version.BuildVariantCommunity {
+		klog.Infof("LVMS is not deployed by community builds")
+		return false, nil
+	}
+
 	cfgFile := "/etc/microshift/lvmd.yaml"
 	if exists, err := util.PathExists(cfgFile); err != nil {
 		return false, err
